WEBVTT

00:00:32.908 --> 00:00:35.911
Oh, Lordy Lou! Help!

00:00:36.745 --> 00:00:38.247
Ooh! Ah!

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:41.625
I know you've rejected me
a lot before,

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:44.545
but frankly, I wasn't sure
we were right for each other, either.

00:00:44.628 --> 00:00:48.173
But now I am, so how about a date tonight?

00:00:48.257 --> 00:00:52.553
Sorry, I think I, uh,
I think I left my toaster on.

00:00:52.636 --> 00:00:54.054
Buddha! Zeus!

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:57.474
God! One of you guys, do something!

00:00:57.558 --> 00:00:58.851
Come on, Leela.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.019
What's the real reason
you won't go out with me?

00:01:01.103 --> 00:01:04.064
Help, Satan, you owe me!

00:01:04.147 --> 00:01:06.859
Look, um, I'm embarrassed to admit this,

00:01:06.942 --> 00:01:08.861
but you've forced me to.

00:01:08.944 --> 00:01:10.654
I can't go out tonight because...

00:01:11.864 --> 00:01:14.157
I have sweaty boot rash!

00:01:14.491 --> 00:01:16.535
No spluh. Why do you think

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:18.829
I'm sitting over here
in the stink-free zone?

00:01:20.247 --> 00:01:22.040
So, will you go out with me?

00:01:22.374 --> 00:01:24.042
Good news, everyone.

00:01:24.126 --> 00:01:26.962
I'm still technically alive. Yes.

00:01:27.045 --> 00:01:30.966
But I need you to dispose
of this crazy-ass experiment

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:32.467
that almost killed me.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.721
You'll have to throw it
into the sun itself

00:01:35.804 --> 00:01:38.682
for only the thermonuclear
inferno of the sun

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:42.311
has enough energy to ensure
its total destruction.

00:01:42.394 --> 00:01:43.812
I could hit it with a shovel.

00:01:43.896 --> 00:01:45.105
That's not good enough.

00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:47.065
This one time, I pounded a guy

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:49.026
into the ground
like a stake with a shovel.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.152
Yes, yes.

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:51.695
So what's in the box already?

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:52.905
No peeking!

00:01:55.032 --> 00:01:56.992
I don't know what's in there,

00:01:57.075 --> 00:02:00.746
but I'm sure our minds
would be unable to comprehend it.

00:02:01.163 --> 00:02:03.624
Oh! You hurt my collator!

00:02:03.707 --> 00:02:04.917
I don't care.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.335
Listen well.

00:02:06.418 --> 00:02:10.297
No matter what happens,
no matter how great your curiosity,

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.133
you are forbidden to look in this box.

00:02:13.217 --> 00:02:14.718
Forbidden!

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.845
Pretty tantalizing, though.

00:02:18.555 --> 00:02:21.308
Whatever's in there,
it's the only thing I've ever wanted.

00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:24.353
In my experience, boxes are usually empty,

00:02:24.436 --> 00:02:26.939
or maybe with a little cheese
stuck to the top,

00:02:27.022 --> 00:02:28.815
and one time, pepperoni.

00:02:28.899 --> 00:02:30.609
What a day that was!

00:02:32.319 --> 00:02:33.570
Give me the box!

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.573
Scram, you lousy green snakes!

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:42.412
Here, Leela, take this
and use it to shoot those guys.

00:02:42.496 --> 00:02:44.790
Right. If they try to look in the box.

00:02:44.915 --> 00:02:45.958
Whatever.

00:02:46.542 --> 00:02:48.085
Let's just forget about the box.

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:50.170
The professor said to stay away.

00:02:50.254 --> 00:02:52.923
Fry, how can you be so naive?

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:54.967
He was joking. Get it?

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.134
No.

00:02:56.218 --> 00:02:58.387
That's what makes it so funny.

00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:02.015
Okay, he wasn't joking.

00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:03.684
Now shut up and follow me.

00:03:10.315 --> 00:03:11.733
Ow, it's hot.

00:03:11.817 --> 00:03:13.443
The butter in my pocket is melting.

00:03:34.923 --> 00:03:37.384
Yup.

00:03:44.808 --> 00:03:48.604
We thank you, Bender,
for the gift we are about to receive.

00:03:52.566 --> 00:03:54.109
Tangled-up Christmas lights.

00:03:54.193 --> 00:03:55.903
We can take shifts untangling them.

00:03:55.986 --> 00:03:57.321
And unlabeled booze.

00:03:57.404 --> 00:03:59.156
Wide mouth, too.

00:04:03.577 --> 00:04:05.746
That ought to keep those dopes occupied.

00:04:05.829 --> 00:04:10.417
I can guard the real box in peace
now that no one's curious about it.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:39.696
Well, I got through the night
and no one looked in the box,

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.116
not even me, the person
who gave up her whole evening

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.243
to watch it.

00:04:44.326 --> 00:04:46.537
A whole evening of TV gone.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:50.582
What a mockery of justice
that I can't take even a little tiny peek.

00:04:51.208 --> 00:04:53.418
I need coffee.

00:04:59.466 --> 00:05:02.427
Okay, heads, I look. Tails, I don't.

00:05:05.597 --> 00:05:08.225
Oh, yeah! Oh, yeah! Heads!

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:09.935
I mean, all right, then.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:14.147
No. I have a duty not to look.

00:05:15.023 --> 00:05:18.068
Then again, I promised the coin I would.

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:24.283
Oh, it's deep.

00:05:24.366 --> 00:05:26.535
Deeper than a small box should be.

00:05:30.414 --> 00:05:33.375
Ouch! My lawyer will hear about this.

00:05:33.458 --> 00:05:35.836
Leela, what have you done?

00:05:35.919 --> 00:05:38.422
Nothing. What do you mean,
why was I looking in the box?

00:05:38.505 --> 00:05:41.175
I meant you hair. It's all differenty.

00:05:41.258 --> 00:05:43.552
Bender, is that you?

00:05:43.635 --> 00:05:45.888
You know it. Large and in charge.

00:05:46.388 --> 00:05:48.432
Leela? Oh...

00:05:48.515 --> 00:05:50.017
There's a woman for you.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:53.353
Always dyeing her hair
instead of not looking in a box.

00:05:53.437 --> 00:05:55.147
I didn't dye my hair.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:56.607
This is how I always look.

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:58.775
No, that's how you always look.

00:06:02.571 --> 00:06:06.617
This throws my entire perception
of reality into question.

00:06:06.992 --> 00:06:10.120
Clone, robot or long-lost twin?

00:06:10.204 --> 00:06:11.496
Taking all bets.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:13.832
I also offer video poker.

00:06:18.337 --> 00:06:20.172
It's some guy wearing a Leela costume.

00:06:20.255 --> 00:06:21.340
Get him.

00:06:21.423 --> 00:06:24.384
Hold it. You have this all wrong.

00:06:24.468 --> 00:06:27.387
I just fell into the box
and then I fell out somehow.

00:06:27.513 --> 00:06:28.805
You shut up, sir.

00:06:28.889 --> 00:06:30.641
No, wait. I've got it.

00:06:30.724 --> 00:06:32.726
I know what's in the box.

00:06:32.809 --> 00:06:35.312
Oh, I've been as dumb as Fry.

00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:36.438
Am not.

00:06:36.522 --> 00:06:39.775
It contains a parallel universe!

00:06:41.026 --> 00:06:43.612
And when you create a parallel universe,

00:06:43.695 --> 00:06:46.949
it's almost always
populated by evil twins.

00:06:47.032 --> 00:06:49.159
Now, look, I am not evil.

00:06:49.243 --> 00:06:50.744
My loan officer said so.

00:06:50.827 --> 00:06:54.373
Oh, you'd like us to believe that
wouldn't you, Leela?

00:06:54.456 --> 00:06:56.708
Or should I say, Evilla?

00:06:56.792 --> 00:06:58.710
Aw, this is awful.

00:06:58.794 --> 00:07:01.421
Somewhere there's
a more evil Bender than me.

00:07:01.505 --> 00:07:03.257
I do my best, damn it!

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.425
Leela, the good Leela,

00:07:05.509 --> 00:07:08.804
I want you
to snoop around the other universe

00:07:08.887 --> 00:07:10.973
and find out how evil they are.

00:07:12.057 --> 00:07:13.267
Here.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:17.855
I tell you, they're not evil.
But don't be confused, they are jerks.

00:07:19.565 --> 00:07:20.816
Hello.

00:07:20.899 --> 00:07:23.527
- Hi-ya!
- Ow!

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:26.113
Come out of your universe
with your hands up.

00:07:31.451 --> 00:07:34.288
Oh, wow, it's like that drug trip
I saw in that movie

00:07:34.371 --> 00:07:35.789
when I was on that drug trip.

00:07:35.873 --> 00:07:37.124
Astonishing!

00:07:37.207 --> 00:07:39.793
I must have created a parallel universe.

00:07:39.877 --> 00:07:42.671
Baldercrap! I created your universe.

00:07:42.754 --> 00:07:46.216
All you created was my fist
parallel to your face.

00:07:47.134 --> 00:07:48.218
Ow.

00:07:48.302 --> 00:07:50.888
Look, it doesn't matter who created what.

00:07:50.971 --> 00:07:52.347
The important thing is...

00:07:52.431 --> 00:07:53.473
Hi-ya!

00:07:54.516 --> 00:07:56.143
We're exactly the same.

00:07:56.226 --> 00:07:57.561
I know all her moves.

00:07:57.644 --> 00:07:59.855
Therefore, I've got the upper hand.

00:07:59.938 --> 00:08:01.648
Hi-ya! Ow!

00:08:02.107 --> 00:08:07.029
Now, now, perfectly symmetrical violence
never solved anything.

00:08:08.197 --> 00:08:10.908
Let's recap what's happened so far.

00:08:12.534 --> 00:08:17.372
As you can see, I accidentally created
a box containing your universe.

00:08:17.456 --> 00:08:20.000
While I, in a simultaneous blunder,

00:08:20.083 --> 00:08:22.711
created a box containing your universe.

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:24.922
This is getting confusing.

00:08:25.005 --> 00:08:27.466
Why don't we call
our universe "Universe A"

00:08:27.549 --> 00:08:29.343
and this universe "Universe B"?

00:08:29.426 --> 00:08:32.095
Hey, why can't we be "Universe A"?

00:08:32.179 --> 00:08:33.180
Yeah!

00:08:33.263 --> 00:08:34.264
- Yeah!
- It's the best letter!

00:08:34.348 --> 00:08:35.432
We called it first.

00:08:35.516 --> 00:08:38.060
Besides, this place kind of feels
like a "B," you know?

00:08:38.143 --> 00:08:40.854
All right, you can be crummy "Universe A"

00:08:40.938 --> 00:08:42.731
and we'll be "Universe One."

00:08:42.814 --> 00:08:45.609
Or "The Mongooses."
That's a cool team name.

00:08:45.692 --> 00:08:47.319
"The Fighting Mongooses."

00:08:47.402 --> 00:08:48.445
Wait a second.

00:08:48.529 --> 00:08:52.074
If everyone is identical
why did our Leela look into the box

00:08:52.157 --> 00:08:53.700
and your Leela didn't?

00:08:53.784 --> 00:08:56.370
Well, to be honest, I tossed a coin.

00:08:56.453 --> 00:08:58.163
It came up tails, so I didn't look.

00:08:58.288 --> 00:08:59.373
That's weird.

00:08:59.456 --> 00:09:01.333
Mine came up heads, so I did.

00:09:01.416 --> 00:09:02.793
Interesting.

00:09:02.876 --> 00:09:05.754
Apparently, the key difference
between our universes

00:09:05.838 --> 00:09:08.173
is that coin flips have opposite outcomes.

00:09:08.257 --> 00:09:10.175
That explains Fruity here.

00:09:10.259 --> 00:09:12.845
I tossed a coin to pick my finish.

00:09:12.928 --> 00:09:14.179
Foghat Gray.

00:09:14.263 --> 00:09:17.015
Hey, bite my glorious golden ass.

00:09:17.099 --> 00:09:19.643
You people and your
slight differences disgust me.

00:09:19.726 --> 00:09:20.853
I'm going home.

00:09:20.936 --> 00:09:24.690
Where's that blue box
with our universe in it?

00:09:24.773 --> 00:09:28.485
Oh, you'd like to get back
to your evil universe, wouldn't you,

00:09:28.569 --> 00:09:31.280
and destroy your box
with our universe inside it?

00:09:31.363 --> 00:09:32.447
Nonsense.

00:09:32.531 --> 00:09:34.283
I would never do such a thing

00:09:34.366 --> 00:09:37.244
unless you were already having
been going to do that.

00:09:37.327 --> 00:09:38.412
Wha...

00:09:38.495 --> 00:09:39.580
You heard me.

00:09:39.663 --> 00:09:41.748
In any case, I've hidden the box,

00:09:41.832 --> 00:09:45.335
and it will remain hidden
until I'm convinced you're not evil.

00:09:45.419 --> 00:09:48.547
Everyone, keep an eye
on your evil counterpart.

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:50.257
And you all do the same.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:53.760
Um, can Fry and I watch
our parallel selves together?

00:09:53.844 --> 00:09:55.220
We have plans tonight.

00:09:55.304 --> 00:09:56.930
You guys are dating?

00:09:57.014 --> 00:09:58.182
Oh, no, no.

00:09:58.307 --> 00:09:59.391
We're married.

00:10:07.274 --> 00:10:09.109
I got my eye on you, boy.

00:10:09.193 --> 00:10:11.361
Don't even think about it, lunch pail.

00:10:11.445 --> 00:10:13.447
You'd be dead before you hit the ground.

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:14.531
Good point.

00:10:14.615 --> 00:10:16.283
What do you say we just hit a strip joint?

00:10:16.366 --> 00:10:18.493
I was waiting for one of us to say that.

00:10:20.454 --> 00:10:23.332
Bender A, you're a prince among robots.

00:10:23.415 --> 00:10:25.501
Can you forgive me for distrusting you?

00:10:25.584 --> 00:10:29.463
Aw, I can't stay mad at
what is essentially me.

00:10:29.546 --> 00:10:30.797
I love me.

00:10:34.885 --> 00:10:37.095
This is so great!

00:10:37.179 --> 00:10:39.848
I always wanted an imaginary friend.

00:10:39.932 --> 00:10:42.392
I'm not imaginary, I'm parallel.

00:10:42.476 --> 00:10:44.770
We're exactly the same,
right down to the...

00:10:44.853 --> 00:10:47.564
Splech! Is that pink nail polish?

00:10:47.648 --> 00:10:49.608
Is that not pink nail polish?

00:10:49.691 --> 00:10:52.903
The professor's right, you are evil,

00:10:52.986 --> 00:10:54.196
and shallow.

00:10:54.279 --> 00:10:55.948
I am not evil.

00:10:59.034 --> 00:11:02.079
So, Fry, Leela,
how'd you two get together?

00:11:02.162 --> 00:11:03.330
Funny story.

00:11:03.413 --> 00:11:06.124
I asked Leela out a million times
but she just kept rejecting me.

00:11:06.208 --> 00:11:09.253
I'd make up stuff like
"I have sweaty boot rash"

00:11:09.336 --> 00:11:11.129
or "I have to meet the president."

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:15.175
Oh, man, you never heard such excuses.

00:11:15.259 --> 00:11:17.302
But, like a dope, I believed her.

00:11:17.386 --> 00:11:20.138
Looking back on it now,
it's kind of funny.

00:11:20.222 --> 00:11:21.306
It sure is.

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:23.976
Right, Leela? Funny. Ha, ha, ha, ha.

00:11:24.059 --> 00:11:26.353
Then one night, when Fry asked me out,

00:11:26.436 --> 00:11:28.897
the only excuse I could think of
involved ghosts.

00:11:28.981 --> 00:11:30.190
I knew he wouldn't buy it.

00:11:30.274 --> 00:11:32.442
So, I did what I always do
in those situations.

00:11:32.526 --> 00:11:33.610
Oh, Lord.

00:11:33.694 --> 00:11:34.903
I flipped a coin.

00:11:34.987 --> 00:11:37.239
It came up heads and we went out.

00:11:37.322 --> 00:11:40.367
You mean, you flipped a coin, too,
and it was tails?

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.911
So, that's why you said
you had to meet that ghost.

00:11:42.995 --> 00:11:44.997
You really missed out on something, Leela.

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:46.582
That date was magical.

00:11:46.665 --> 00:11:49.376
One year later, I gave Leela
a diamond scrunchy

00:11:49.459 --> 00:11:50.502
and we were married.

00:11:50.586 --> 00:11:51.920
Ooh...

00:11:52.004 --> 00:11:55.132
One year later, I got beat up
at a Neil Diamond concert

00:11:55.215 --> 00:11:56.800
by a guy named Scrunchy.

00:12:04.183 --> 00:12:05.893
Well, that was pointless.

00:12:05.976 --> 00:12:08.687
Say, I hope you won't
think it "evil" of me

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:11.481
to ask how you got
that stylish head wound.

00:12:11.565 --> 00:12:13.192
Oh, this old thing?

00:12:13.275 --> 00:12:16.904
I was experimenting to see
if I could remove my own brain.

00:12:16.987 --> 00:12:19.406
Of course. I had the same idea.

00:12:19.489 --> 00:12:21.867
I flipped a coin to decide
if I should proceed

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:23.076
but it came up tails.

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:24.203
So, I didn't.

00:12:24.286 --> 00:12:25.537
How'd it go?

00:12:25.621 --> 00:12:28.624
Well, getting the brain out
was the easy part.

00:12:28.707 --> 00:12:31.543
The hard part was getting the brain out.

00:12:33.003 --> 00:12:34.213
Oh, you.

00:12:36.715 --> 00:12:38.842
So, tell me about yourself.

00:12:38.926 --> 00:12:40.260
Well, don't look into it,

00:12:40.344 --> 00:12:42.971
but I'm a respected
internal medicine doctor.

00:12:43.055 --> 00:12:44.598
Ooh, a can!

00:12:47.476 --> 00:12:50.896
As for me, I design mansions,
then live in them.

00:12:50.979 --> 00:12:53.690
I'm lying.

00:12:53.774 --> 00:12:55.943
I'm an appalling failure.

00:12:56.026 --> 00:12:58.320
Me, too.

00:12:58.403 --> 00:12:59.821
A big fat one.

00:12:59.905 --> 00:13:01.240
And those coworkers,

00:13:01.323 --> 00:13:03.825
always looking down on us Zoidbergs.

00:13:03.909 --> 00:13:05.744
What are they, from Nob Hill?

00:13:05.827 --> 00:13:09.122
They're all like,
"Stop spraying me with ink, Zoidberg.

00:13:09.206 --> 00:13:10.958
"Put on pants, Zoidberg.

00:13:11.041 --> 00:13:13.418
"Don't touch our fancy box, Zoidberg."

00:13:13.502 --> 00:13:15.504
Ooh, that box!

00:13:15.587 --> 00:13:16.713
Too good for us, is it?

00:13:16.797 --> 00:13:20.551
Bah! Someday they'll watch
from down in the gutter, they will,

00:13:20.634 --> 00:13:23.720
as King Zoidberg caresses their fancy box.

00:13:24.304 --> 00:13:29.601
You know, maybe a certain blue lobster
saw where Professor hid the box.

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:38.694
Good news, everyones.

00:13:38.777 --> 00:13:40.779
After carefully reading the scriptures,

00:13:40.863 --> 00:13:43.615
we've concluded that none of us are evil.

00:13:43.782 --> 00:13:46.785
Yes, the Bible is the real "good news."

00:13:46.869 --> 00:13:50.664
Anyhow, you're all free
to go back to your own universe.

00:13:51.665 --> 00:13:52.958
What's going on here?

00:13:53.041 --> 00:13:55.544
Why aren't you all out
destroying the professor's box?

00:13:55.627 --> 00:13:57.254
Hermes, aren't you curious

00:13:57.337 --> 00:13:59.006
about the fact
that there's two of everybody?

00:13:59.089 --> 00:14:01.300
No. Now, like my granny used to say

00:14:01.383 --> 00:14:03.969
back in her tarpaper shack on Montego Bay,

00:14:04.052 --> 00:14:06.305
"If you want a box hurled into the sun,

00:14:06.388 --> 00:14:07.973
"you got to do it yourself."

00:14:08.056 --> 00:14:09.641
Your granny can go to hell.

00:14:09.725 --> 00:14:12.144
I've hidden the box so no one can destroy

00:14:12.227 --> 00:14:14.730
the home universe
of my handsome friend here.

00:14:14.813 --> 00:14:16.023
Oh, go on.

00:14:16.106 --> 00:14:17.274
Wait a second.

00:14:17.357 --> 00:14:18.775
If your Hermes was

00:14:18.859 --> 00:14:21.862
about to destroy the box
containing our universe...

00:14:21.945 --> 00:14:24.156
Then your Hermes...

00:14:24.239 --> 00:14:25.991
Oh, my.

00:14:26.074 --> 00:14:28.076
And sure enough...

00:14:29.912 --> 00:14:31.371
Like Granny said,

00:14:31.455 --> 00:14:33.415
"If you want a box hurled into the sun,

00:14:33.498 --> 00:14:35.042
"you got to do it yourself."

00:14:36.251 --> 00:14:38.462
God rest her zombie bones.

00:14:42.132 --> 00:14:44.593
So we go back through the box
and stop Hermes.

00:14:44.676 --> 00:14:48.972
Right. Good thing Professor B there
hid it in the coelacanth tank.

00:14:49.056 --> 00:14:51.725
No one but a crazy lobster
would look there.

00:14:53.602 --> 00:14:54.811
It's gone!

00:14:57.105 --> 00:14:58.941
All hail Zoidberg,

00:14:59.024 --> 00:15:00.484
the king with the box.

00:15:03.028 --> 00:15:05.030
Now it's my turn maybe?

00:15:05.113 --> 00:15:07.241
The box says no.

00:15:09.743 --> 00:15:11.995
Meanwhile, in Universe A,

00:15:12.079 --> 00:15:15.791
Hermes A heads toward the sun... A.

00:15:16.416 --> 00:15:18.043
"Item one, box."

00:15:18.502 --> 00:15:19.586
Check.

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:21.213
"Item two, sun."

00:15:22.965 --> 00:15:24.424
Ooh, that's a big check.

00:15:25.884 --> 00:15:27.094
Ooh!

00:15:40.482 --> 00:15:43.402
If I know parallel Hermes,
he's at the sun by now.

00:15:43.485 --> 00:15:46.238
Our universe is doomed!

00:15:46.321 --> 00:15:49.658
Doomed!

00:15:49.741 --> 00:15:52.369
Now, don't give up yet, you crybabies.

00:15:52.452 --> 00:15:56.874
The box is gone, but we still have
one preposterously slim hope.

00:15:56.957 --> 00:15:58.584
Is it a kind of hair spray?

00:15:58.667 --> 00:16:01.003
No! We must attempt to make

00:16:01.086 --> 00:16:04.923
another box containing our universe. Doy.

00:16:17.603 --> 00:16:19.730
Well, is that your universes in there?

00:16:19.813 --> 00:16:21.356
Nope. Too cold.

00:16:23.609 --> 00:16:25.485
Hmm. All women.

00:16:25.569 --> 00:16:28.113
I'll put this one aside for later.

00:16:31.158 --> 00:16:32.868
Oh, mon, it's hopeless.

00:16:32.951 --> 00:16:35.287
We'll never find your universe in time.

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:37.789
Plus, this box is stuck on my fat head.

00:16:37.873 --> 00:16:40.125
Yes, it's the apocalypse, all right.

00:16:40.209 --> 00:16:42.711
I always thought I'd have a hand in it.

00:16:42.794 --> 00:16:44.129
I'm not sad,

00:16:44.213 --> 00:16:46.965
because I finally found
someone as great as me.

00:16:47.049 --> 00:16:49.051
It's like I always say,

00:16:49.134 --> 00:16:51.345
"Make new friends, but keep the old.

00:16:51.428 --> 00:16:52.888
"One is silver..."

00:16:52.971 --> 00:16:55.015
"And the other's gold."

00:17:00.145 --> 00:17:02.022
Why with the long faces?

00:17:02.314 --> 00:17:04.358
The idiots have the box!

00:17:04.441 --> 00:17:06.318
I think she means you.

00:17:06.401 --> 00:17:07.444
Grab them!

00:17:11.949 --> 00:17:14.326
You coward! Wait for me!

00:17:21.166 --> 00:17:23.877
Blug! Which one did they go into?

00:17:23.961 --> 00:17:26.046
Oh, let's all ask each other!

00:17:26.129 --> 00:17:28.131
That'll solve this problem!

00:17:28.215 --> 00:17:30.509
We'll each have to search a universe.

00:17:30.592 --> 00:17:34.763
Everyone grab a length of wire first
so you can find your way back.

00:17:51.613 --> 00:17:52.698
Hello?

00:17:52.781 --> 00:17:54.616
Did you see two smelly lobsters?

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:57.369
We didn't see anything...

00:17:58.245 --> 00:17:59.413
Ever.

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:05.961
Yo, uh, did two shellfish in scrubs go by?

00:18:06.044 --> 00:18:07.462
- Hell, no.
- Shut up.

00:18:07.546 --> 00:18:09.047
Beat it, jerk!

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:16.221
Uh, have you robot versions of you guys

00:18:16.305 --> 00:18:18.307
seen any extra Zoidbergs around here?

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:20.934
Negative.
Will you go out with me?

00:18:21.018 --> 00:18:23.020
Uh, access denied.

00:18:29.276 --> 00:18:32.029
Hey, pal, look what I snagged
from the leprechaun universe.

00:18:33.655 --> 00:18:36.074
Yeah, leprechaun universe is fine,

00:18:36.158 --> 00:18:38.952
if you haven't seen pirate universe.

00:18:40.662 --> 00:18:42.372
Faith and Begorra!

00:18:44.833 --> 00:18:45.834
Que?

00:18:47.461 --> 00:18:49.254
Quick! Into another box!

00:18:49.338 --> 00:18:51.507
There aren't any in this universe,
there aren't.

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:53.592
Hey, you, what with the no boxes?

00:18:53.675 --> 00:18:55.427
Baby, they're somewhere.

00:18:55.511 --> 00:18:57.387
Everything's, like, somewhere.

00:18:57.471 --> 00:18:59.890
Place is kind of au naturel right now.

00:19:01.475 --> 00:19:02.726
There they are!

00:19:03.936 --> 00:19:05.020
Gotcha!

00:19:05.604 --> 00:19:10.067
Dig it, all of you fitting in this box
is, like, seriously freaked up.

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:13.362
Nonsense! Why, there's
a whole universe in there.

00:19:13.612 --> 00:19:16.949
Dude, there's a universe in all of us.

00:19:17.199 --> 00:19:19.451
Right on, Professor Freaksworth!

00:19:21.495 --> 00:19:22.496
Get a job!

00:19:23.622 --> 00:19:24.748
We've got the box!

00:19:24.831 --> 00:19:26.333
Everyone pull your wires!

00:19:35.634 --> 00:19:38.136
Hurry! Back to Universe A!

00:20:03.495 --> 00:20:06.039
Hermes! Don't press that button!

00:20:12.296 --> 00:20:13.505
Okay.

00:20:16.091 --> 00:20:17.843
- Bye, Leela.
- Bye-bye.

00:20:17.926 --> 00:20:20.429
- So long.
- So long, Your Majesty.

00:20:25.684 --> 00:20:28.145
There but for the flip of a coin go we.

00:20:28.687 --> 00:20:32.524
So, um, Leela, seeing how
the universe wasn't destroyed,

00:20:32.608 --> 00:20:34.276
uh, you want to catch an ape fight?

00:20:34.359 --> 00:20:35.736
You know, together?

00:20:36.195 --> 00:20:39.448
Well, I guess you deserve one more flip.

00:20:42.075 --> 00:20:43.785
So? Heads or tails?

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:47.039
You know, let's just say it's heads.

00:20:49.958 --> 00:20:51.001
Ready?

00:20:51.084 --> 00:20:54.963
One, two, three, pull!

00:20:57.841 --> 00:20:58.884
There.

00:20:58.967 --> 00:21:04.097
That space-time eversion
has given us their box, and vice versa.

00:21:04.515 --> 00:21:07.059
So what you think you just
explained to us is that...

00:21:07.142 --> 00:21:11.271
Correct! This box contains
our own universe!

00:21:13.232 --> 00:21:14.983
Sweet honeybee of infinity!

00:21:22.866 --> 00:21:25.077
Bender, quit destroying the universe.

00:21:26.203 --> 00:21:27.955
But... Oh!

00:21:28.455 --> 00:21:32.668
Yes, all that is and ever shall be
is in that box.

00:21:33.126 --> 00:21:35.921
And the box itself
is probably worth something, too.

00:21:36.004 --> 00:21:37.422
We must cherish it

00:21:37.506 --> 00:21:40.384
as we cherish every moment of our lives.